  "chapter": {
    "number": 51,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(52) For the end, a Psalm of",
          {
            "noteId": 98
          },
          "instruction by David, when Doec the Idumean came and told Saul, and said to him, David is gone to the house of Abimelech."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Why do you, O mighty man, boast of iniquity in your mischief? All the day",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "your tongue has devised unrighteousness; like a sharpened razor you have wrought deceit.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have loved wickedness more than goodness; unrighteousness better than to speak righteousness. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have loved all words of destruction, and a deceitful tongue.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore may God destroy you for ever, may he pluck you up and utterly remove you from your dwelling, and your root from the land of the living. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And the righteous shall see, and fear, and shall laugh at him, and say,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Behold the man who made not God his help; but trusted in the abundance of his wealth, and strengthened himself in his vanity.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But I am as a fruitful olive in the house of God: I have trusted in the mercy of God for ever, even for evermore.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I will give thanks to you for ever, for you have done it: and I will wait on your name; for it is good before the saints.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
